    <artifactId>VegaModels-DevtoxCaesar</artifactId>
    <version>2.2.0</version>

    <!--
        Up to version 2.1.9 this model depended on weka:weka:3.5.8, an artifact from 2008 that is not on Maven
        Central: it was served only by http://obsearch.net/repository/, an HTTP-only repository that recent Maven
        versions block, and had to be republished on the ProtoQSAR Nexus to stay resolvable. WEKA was used to
        train the random forest again on every instantiation of the model, which also made the predictions depend
        on the floating point library of the JVM that ran the training. The trained forest has been extracted
        once, with tools/weka-forest-dump, and now lives in /data/forest_devtox_caesar.txt: the model reads it and
        predicts on its own, with no dependency left. The predictions are unchanged, as the regression tests show.
    -->


    <name>Developmental Toxicity model (CAESAR)</name>
    <description>
        QSAR classification model for Developmental Toxicity (from CAESAR project)
    </description>


